{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1372446-leeching-willpower","id":1372446,"title":"Leeching Willpower","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-03T06:31:18-08:00","id":1372446,"title":"Leeching Willpower","content":"What level of Mind would be required to steal Willpower from a victim and absorb it into one self?<br /> <br /> My guess is 5 dots (in essence stripping away their mind and adding it to my own) but I thought one of the revised era books actually mentioned this, or at least mentioned outright stripping Willpower from another.<br /> <br /> Of course this is for a Nephandus and not my PC. I'm not &quot;that&quot; wicked when playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T10:46:05-08:00","id":1372498,"title":"","content":"Iteration X 1st ed page 48 describes it as using Mind 2 to temporarily reduce Willpower for the duration of the effect, and it is actually resisted with a Willpower roll diff 7.<br /> It is a sort of Rote that is aimed at humiliating or depressing the victim, and that's a case where Mind 2 makes very much sense, as it is used to affect emotions - however, this is a social rote, not a combat rote.<br /> <br /> Similiar NWO 1st ed also uses Mind 2 for a sort of psychic weaking of resolve.<br /> <br /> Syndicate 1st ed has a similiar psychic rote, though this one uses Life 3 + Mind 3 to have a Syndicate agent *describe* the horrible things they could do to somebody captured, and resisting lowers willpower by 1 for every hour passing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, these are all 1st ed, but the Sphere levels quite make sense - Mind 2 for the first two is all about emotions, and there is nothing worse to shatter your resolve temporarily than a feeling of apathy, depression, sad desparation or essential uselessness of your acts.<br /> <br /> Mind 3 can take this deeper and actually start affecting your thoughts.<br /> <br /> <br /> The sense of *literally* stealing somebody's Willpower though? Well, it could be the same spheres, really. Imagine stealing somebody's positive emotions, their heroism, their eagerness, infusing it into yourself while filling themselves with apathy? Kind of also Mind 2, really.<br /> <br /> Though if you are talking *permanent*? I would definitely say Mind 5, because as you describe, yes, that would be kind of permanently removing a piece of their mind and adding it to your own.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T15:43:42-08:00","id":1372558,"title":"","content":"Much thanks for all the references. I didn't think about Temporary Willpower being an easier endeavor. Actually it was all I was looking for though so these types of Rotes are perfect.<br /> <br /> Thanks again. This just might be my most hated villain yet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}